=head2 Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::NodeConfig

Parameters that describe the nodes in a cluster.

GKE Autopilot clusters do not
recognize parameters in `NodeConfig`. Use
[AutoprovisioningNodePoolDefaults][google.container.v1beta1.AutoprovisioningNodePoolDefaults]
instead.

Inherits from L<Protobuf::Message>.

=head3 Accessors

=over 4

=item * C<< $msg->machine_type() >> / C<< $msg->machine_type($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The name of a Google Compute Engine [machine
type](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/machine-types).

If unspecified, the default machine type is
`e2-medium`.

=item * C<< $msg->disk_size_gb() >> / C<< $msg->disk_size_gb($value) >>

Type: C<Int32>

Size of the disk attached to each node, specified in GB.
The smallest allowed disk size is 10GB.

If unspecified, the default disk size is 100GB.

=item * C<< $msg->oauth_scopes() >> / C<< $msg->oauth_scopes($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The set of Google API scopes to be made available on all of the
node VMs under the "default" service account.

The following scopes are recommended, but not required, and by default are
not included:

* `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/compute` is required for mounting
persistent storage on your nodes.
* `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/devstorage.read_only` is required for
communicating with B<gcr.io>
(the [Artifact Registry](https://cloud.google.com/artifact-registry/)).

If unspecified, no scopes are added, unless Cloud Logging or Cloud
Monitoring are enabled, in which case their required scopes will be added.

=item * C<< $msg->service_account() >> / C<< $msg->service_account($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The Google Cloud Platform Service Account to be used by the node VMs.
Specify the email address of the Service Account; otherwise, if no Service
Account is specified, the "default" service account is used.

=item * C<< $msg->metadata() >> / C<< $msg->metadata($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::NodeConfig::MetadataEntry>)

The metadata key/value pairs assigned to instances in the cluster.

Keys must conform to the regexp `[a-zA-Z0-9-_]+` and be less than 128 bytes
in length. These are reflected as part of a URL in the metadata server.
Additionally, to avoid ambiguity, keys must not conflict with any other
metadata keys for the project or be one of the reserved keys:

 - "cluster-location"
 - "cluster-name"
 - "cluster-uid"
 - "configure-sh"
 - "containerd-configure-sh"
 - "enable-oslogin"
 - "gci-ensure-gke-docker"
 - "gci-metrics-enabled"
 - "gci-update-strategy"
 - "instance-template"
 - "kube-env"
 - "startup-script"
 - "user-data"
 - "disable-address-manager"
 - "windows-startup-script-ps1"
 - "common-psm1"
 - "k8s-node-setup-psm1"
 - "install-ssh-psm1"
 - "user-profile-psm1"

Values are free-form strings, and only have meaning as interpreted by
the image running in the instance. The only restriction placed on them is
that each value's size must be less than or equal to 32 KB.

The total size of all keys and values must be less than 512 KB.

=item * C<< $msg->image_type() >> / C<< $msg->image_type($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The image type to use for this node. Note that for a given image type,
the latest version of it will be used. Please see
https://cloud.google.com/kubernetes-engine/docs/concepts/node-images
for available image types.

=item * C<< $msg->node_image_config() >> / C<< $msg->node_image_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::CustomImageConfig>)

The node image configuration to use for this node pool.  Note that this is
only applicable for node pools using image_type=CUSTOM.

=item * C<< $msg->labels() >> / C<< $msg->labels($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::NodeConfig::LabelsEntry>)

The Kubernetes labels (key/value pairs) to apply to each node. The values
in this field are added to the set of default labels Kubernetes applies to
nodes.

This field has the following restrictions:

* Labels must use a valid Kubernetes syntax and character set, as defined
  in
  https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/overview/working-with-objects/labels/#syntax-and-character-set.
* This field supports up to 1,024 total characters in a single request.

Depending on the Kubernetes version, keys in this field might conflict with
the keys of the default labels, which might change which of your labels
are applied to the nodes. Assume that the behavior is unpredictable and
avoid label key conflicts. For more information about the default labels,
see:
https://kubernetes.io/docs/reference/labels-annotations-taints/

=item * C<< $msg->local_ssd_count() >> / C<< $msg->local_ssd_count($value) >>

Type: C<Int32>

The number of local SSD disks to be attached to the node.

The limit for this value is dependent upon the maximum number of
disks available on a machine per zone. See:
https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/disks/local-ssd
for more information.

=item * C<< $msg->tags() >> / C<< $msg->tags($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The list of instance tags applied to all nodes. Tags are used to identify
valid sources or targets for network firewalls and are specified by
the client during cluster or node pool creation. Each tag within the list
must comply with RFC1035.

=item * C<< $msg->preemptible() >> / C<< $msg->preemptible($value) >>

Type: C<Bool>

Whether the nodes are created as preemptible VM instances. See:
https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/instances/preemptible
for more information about preemptible VM instances.

=item * C<< $msg->accelerators() >> / C<< $msg->accelerators($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::AcceleratorConfig>)

A list of hardware accelerators to be attached to each node.
See
https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/gpus
for more information about support for GPUs.

=item * C<< $msg->sandbox_config() >> / C<< $msg->sandbox_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::SandboxConfig>)

Sandbox configuration for this node.

=item * C<< $msg->node_group() >> / C<< $msg->node_group($value) >>

Type: C<String>

Setting this field will assign instances of this
pool to run on the specified node group. This is useful for running
workloads on [sole tenant
nodes](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/nodes/sole-tenant-nodes).

=item * C<< $msg->reservation_affinity() >> / C<< $msg->reservation_affinity($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::ReservationAffinity>)

The optional reservation affinity. Setting this field will apply
the specified [Zonal Compute
Reservation](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/instances/reserving-zonal-resources)
to this node pool.

=item * C<< $msg->disk_type() >> / C<< $msg->disk_type($value) >>

Type: C<String>

Type of the disk attached to each node (e.g. 'pd-standard', 'pd-ssd' or
'pd-balanced')

If unspecified, the default disk type is 'pd-standard'

=item * C<< $msg->min_cpu_platform() >> / C<< $msg->min_cpu_platform($value) >>

Type: C<String>

Minimum CPU platform to be used by this instance. The instance may be
scheduled on the specified or newer CPU platform. Applicable values are the
friendly names of CPU platforms, such as
`minCpuPlatform: "Intel Haswell"` or
`minCpuPlatform: "Intel Sandy Bridge"`. For more
information, read [how to specify min CPU
platform](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/instances/specify-min-cpu-platform).

=item * C<< $msg->workload_metadata_config() >> / C<< $msg->workload_metadata_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::WorkloadMetadataConfig>)

The workload metadata configuration for this node.

=item * C<< $msg->taints() >> / C<< $msg->taints($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::NodeTaint>)

List of kubernetes taints to be applied to each node.

For more information, including usage and the valid values, see:
https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/configuration/taint-and-toleration/

=item * C<< $msg->boot_disk_kms_key() >> / C<< $msg->boot_disk_kms_key($value) >>

Type: C<String>


The Customer Managed Encryption Key used to encrypt the boot disk attached
to each node in the node pool. This should be of the form
projects/[KEY_PROJECT_ID]/locations/[LOCATION]/keyRings/[RING_NAME]/cryptoKeys/[KEY_NAME].
For more information about protecting resources with Cloud KMS Keys please
see:
https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/disks/customer-managed-encryption

=item * C<< $msg->shielded_instance_config() >> / C<< $msg->shielded_instance_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::ShieldedInstanceConfig>)

Shielded Instance options.

=item * C<< $msg->linux_node_config() >> / C<< $msg->linux_node_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::LinuxNodeConfig>)

Parameters that can be configured on Linux nodes.

=item * C<< $msg->kubelet_config() >> / C<< $msg->kubelet_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::NodeKubeletConfig>)

Node kubelet configs.

=item * C<< $msg->ephemeral_storage_config() >> / C<< $msg->ephemeral_storage_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::EphemeralStorageConfig>)

Parameters for the ephemeral storage filesystem.
If unspecified, ephemeral storage is backed by the boot disk.

=item * C<< $msg->gcfs_config() >> / C<< $msg->gcfs_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::GcfsConfig>)

GCFS (Google Container File System) configs.

=item * C<< $msg->advanced_machine_features() >> / C<< $msg->advanced_machine_features($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::AdvancedMachineFeatures>)

Advanced features for the Compute Engine VM.

=item * C<< $msg->gvnic() >> / C<< $msg->gvnic($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::VirtualNIC>)

Enable or disable gvnic on the node pool.

=item * C<< $msg->spot() >> / C<< $msg->spot($value) >>

Type: C<Bool>

Spot flag for enabling Spot VM, which is a rebrand of
the existing preemptible flag.

=item * C<< $msg->confidential_nodes() >> / C<< $msg->confidential_nodes($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::ConfidentialNodes>)

Confidential nodes config.
All the nodes in the node pool will be Confidential VM once enabled.

=item * C<< $msg->fast_socket() >> / C<< $msg->fast_socket($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::FastSocket>)

Enable or disable NCCL fast socket for the node pool.

=item * C<< $msg->resource_labels() >> / C<< $msg->resource_labels($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::NodeConfig::ResourceLabelsEntry>)

The resource labels for the node pool to use to annotate any related
Google Compute Engine resources.

=item * C<< $msg->logging_config() >> / C<< $msg->logging_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::NodePoolLoggingConfig>)

Logging configuration.

=item * C<< $msg->windows_node_config() >> / C<< $msg->windows_node_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::WindowsNodeConfig>)

Parameters that can be configured on Windows nodes.

=item * C<< $msg->local_nvme_ssd_block_config() >> / C<< $msg->local_nvme_ssd_block_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::LocalNvmeSsdBlockConfig>)

Parameters for using raw-block Local NVMe SSDs.

=item * C<< $msg->ephemeral_storage_local_ssd_config() >> / C<< $msg->ephemeral_storage_local_ssd_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::EphemeralStorageLocalSsdConfig>)

Parameters for the node ephemeral storage using Local SSDs.
If unspecified, ephemeral storage is backed by the boot disk.
This field is functionally equivalent to the ephemeral_storage_config

=item * C<< $msg->sole_tenant_config() >> / C<< $msg->sole_tenant_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::SoleTenantConfig>)

Parameters for node pools to be backed by shared sole tenant node groups.

=item * C<< $msg->containerd_config() >> / C<< $msg->containerd_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::ContainerdConfig>)

Parameters for containerd customization.

=item * C<< $msg->host_maintenance_policy() >> / C<< $msg->host_maintenance_policy($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::HostMaintenancePolicy>)

HostMaintenancePolicy contains the desired maintenance policy for the
Google Compute Engine hosts.

=item * C<< $msg->resource_manager_tags() >> / C<< $msg->resource_manager_tags($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::ResourceManagerTags>)

A map of resource manager tag keys and values to be attached to the nodes.

=item * C<< $msg->enable_confidential_storage() >> / C<< $msg->enable_confidential_storage($value) >>

Type: C<Bool>

