=head2 Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::IPAllocationPolicy

Configuration for controlling how IPs are allocated in the cluster.

Inherits from L<Protobuf::Message>.

=head3 Accessors

=over 4

=item * C<< $msg->use_ip_aliases() >> / C<< $msg->use_ip_aliases($value) >>

Type: C<Bool>

Whether alias IPs will be used for pod IPs in the cluster.
This is used in conjunction with use_routes. It cannot
be true if use_routes is true. If both use_ip_aliases and use_routes are
false, then the server picks the default IP allocation mode

=item * C<< $msg->create_subnetwork() >> / C<< $msg->create_subnetwork($value) >>

Type: C<Bool>

Whether a new subnetwork will be created automatically for the cluster.

This field is only applicable when `use_ip_aliases` is true.

=item * C<< $msg->subnetwork_name() >> / C<< $msg->subnetwork_name($value) >>

Type: C<String>

A custom subnetwork name to be used if `create_subnetwork` is true.  If
this field is empty, then an automatic name will be chosen for the new
subnetwork.

