=head2 Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::Cluster

A Google Kubernetes Engine cluster.

Inherits from L<Protobuf::Message>.

=head3 Accessors

=over 4

=item * C<< $msg->name() >> / C<< $msg->name($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The name of this cluster. The name must be unique within this project
and location (e.g. zone or region), and can be up to 40 characters with
the following restrictions:

* Lowercase letters, numbers, and hyphens only.
* Must start with a letter.
* Must end with a number or a letter.

=item * C<< $msg->description() >> / C<< $msg->description($value) >>

Type: C<String>

An optional description of this cluster.

=item * C<< $msg->initial_node_count() >> / C<< $msg->initial_node_count($value) >>

Type: C<Int32>

The number of nodes to create in this cluster. You must ensure that your
Compute Engine [resource
quota](https://cloud.google.com/compute/quotas)
is sufficient for this number of instances. You must also have available
firewall and routes quota.
For requests, this field should only be used in lieu of a
"node_pool" object, since this configuration (along with the
"node_config") will be used to create a "NodePool" object with an
auto-generated name. Do not use this and a node_pool at the same time.

This field is deprecated, use node_pool.initial_node_count instead.

=item * C<< $msg->node_config() >> / C<< $msg->node_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::NodeConfig>)

Parameters used in creating the cluster's nodes.
For requests, this field should only be used in lieu of a
"node_pool" object, since this configuration (along with the
"initial_node_count") will be used to create a "NodePool" object with an
auto-generated name. Do not use this and a node_pool at the same time.
For responses, this field will be populated with the node configuration of
the first node pool. (For configuration of each node pool, see
`node_pool.config`)

If unspecified, the defaults are used.
This field is deprecated, use node_pool.config instead.

=item * C<< $msg->master_auth() >> / C<< $msg->master_auth($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::MasterAuth>)

The authentication information for accessing the master endpoint.
If unspecified, the defaults are used:
For clusters before v1.12, if master_auth is unspecified, `username` will
be set to "admin", a random password will be generated, and a client
certificate will be issued.

=item * C<< $msg->logging_service() >> / C<< $msg->logging_service($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The logging service the cluster should use to write logs.
Currently available options:

* `logging.googleapis.com/kubernetes` - The Cloud Logging
service with a Kubernetes-native resource model
* `logging.googleapis.com` - The legacy Cloud Logging service (no longer
  available as of GKE 1.15).
* `none` - no logs will be exported from the cluster.

If left as an empty string,`logging.googleapis.com/kubernetes` will be
used for GKE 1.14+ or `logging.googleapis.com` for earlier versions.

=item * C<< $msg->monitoring_service() >> / C<< $msg->monitoring_service($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The monitoring service the cluster should use to write metrics.
Currently available options:

* `monitoring.googleapis.com/kubernetes` - The Cloud Monitoring
service with a Kubernetes-native resource model
* `monitoring.googleapis.com` - The legacy Cloud Monitoring service (no
  longer available as of GKE 1.15).
* `none` - No metrics will be exported from the cluster.

If left as an empty string,`monitoring.googleapis.com/kubernetes` will be
used for GKE 1.14+ or `monitoring.googleapis.com` for earlier versions.

=item * C<< $msg->network() >> / C<< $msg->network($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The name of the Google Compute Engine
[network](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/networks-and-firewalls#networks)
to which the cluster is connected. If left unspecified, the `default`
network will be used. On output this shows the network ID instead of the
name.

=item * C<< $msg->cluster_ipv4_cidr() >> / C<< $msg->cluster_ipv4_cidr($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The IP address range of the container pods in this cluster, in
[CIDR](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Classless_Inter-Domain_Routing)
notation (e.g. `10.96.0.0/14`). Leave blank to have
one automatically chosen or specify a `/14` block in `10.0.0.0/8`.

=item * C<< $msg->addons_config() >> / C<< $msg->addons_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::AddonsConfig>)

Configurations for the various addons available to run in the cluster.

=item * C<< $msg->subnetwork() >> / C<< $msg->subnetwork($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The name of the Google Compute Engine
[subnetwork](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/subnetworks)
to which the cluster is connected. On output this shows the subnetwork ID
instead of the name.

=item * C<< $msg->node_pools() >> / C<< $msg->node_pools($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::NodePool>)

The node pools associated with this cluster.
This field should not be set if "node_config" or "initial_node_count" are
specified.

=item * C<< $msg->locations() >> / C<< $msg->locations($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The list of Google Compute Engine
[zones](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/zones#available)
in which the cluster's nodes should be located.

This field provides a default value if
[NodePool.Locations](https://cloud.google.com/kubernetes-engine/docs/reference/rest/v1/projects.locations.clusters.nodePools#NodePool.FIELDS.locations)
are not specified during node pool creation.

Warning: changing cluster locations will update the
[NodePool.Locations](https://cloud.google.com/kubernetes-engine/docs/reference/rest/v1/projects.locations.clusters.nodePools#NodePool.FIELDS.locations)
of all node pools and will result in nodes being added and/or removed.

=item * C<< $msg->enable_kubernetes_alpha() >> / C<< $msg->enable_kubernetes_alpha($value) >>

Type: C<Bool>

Kubernetes alpha features are enabled on this cluster. This includes alpha
API groups (e.g. v1beta1) and features that may not be production ready in
the kubernetes version of the master and nodes.
The cluster has no SLA for uptime and master/node upgrades are disabled.
Alpha enabled clusters are automatically deleted thirty days after
creation.

=item * C<< $msg->alpha_cluster_feature_gates() >> / C<< $msg->alpha_cluster_feature_gates($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The list of user specified Kubernetes feature gates.
Each string represents the activation status of a feature gate (e.g.
"featureX=true" or "featureX=false")

=item * C<< $msg->enable_k8s_beta_apis() >> / C<< $msg->enable_k8s_beta_apis($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::K8sBetaAPIConfig>)

Kubernetes open source beta apis enabled on the cluster. Only beta apis.

=item * C<< $msg->resource_labels() >> / C<< $msg->resource_labels($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::Cluster::ResourceLabelsEntry>)

The resource labels for the cluster to use to annotate any related
Google Compute Engine resources.

=item * C<< $msg->label_fingerprint() >> / C<< $msg->label_fingerprint($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The fingerprint of the set of labels for this cluster.

=item * C<< $msg->legacy_abac() >> / C<< $msg->legacy_abac($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::LegacyAbac>)

Configuration for the legacy ABAC authorization mode.

=item * C<< $msg->network_policy() >> / C<< $msg->network_policy($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::NetworkPolicy>)

Configuration options for the NetworkPolicy feature.

=item * C<< $msg->ip_allocation_policy() >> / C<< $msg->ip_allocation_policy($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::IPAllocationPolicy>)

Configuration for cluster IP allocation.

=item * C<< $msg->master_authorized_networks_config() >> / C<< $msg->master_authorized_networks_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::MasterAuthorizedNetworksConfig>)

The configuration options for master authorized networks feature.

Deprecated: Use
[ControlPlaneEndpointsConfig.IPEndpointsConfig.authorized_networks_config][google.container.v1beta1.ControlPlaneEndpointsConfig.IPEndpointsConfig.authorized_networks_config]
instead.

=item * C<< $msg->maintenance_policy() >> / C<< $msg->maintenance_policy($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::MaintenancePolicy>)

Configure the maintenance policy for this cluster.

=item * C<< $msg->binary_authorization() >> / C<< $msg->binary_authorization($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::BinaryAuthorization>)

Configuration for Binary Authorization.

=item * C<< $msg->pod_security_policy_config() >> / C<< $msg->pod_security_policy_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::PodSecurityPolicyConfig>)

Configuration for the PodSecurityPolicy feature.

=item * C<< $msg->autoscaling() >> / C<< $msg->autoscaling($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::ClusterAutoscaling>)

Cluster-level autoscaling configuration.

=item * C<< $msg->network_config() >> / C<< $msg->network_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::NetworkConfig>)

Configuration for cluster networking.

=item * C<< $msg->private_cluster() >> / C<< $msg->private_cluster($value) >>

Type: C<Bool>

If this is a private cluster setup. Private clusters are clusters that, by
default have no external IP addresses on the nodes and where nodes and the
master communicate over private IP addresses.
This field is deprecated, use private_cluster_config.enable_private_nodes
instead.

=item * C<< $msg->master_ipv4_cidr_block() >> / C<< $msg->master_ipv4_cidr_block($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The IP prefix in CIDR notation to use for the hosted master network.
This prefix will be used for assigning private IP addresses to the
master or set of masters, as well as the ILB VIP.
This field is deprecated, use
private_cluster_config.master_ipv4_cidr_block instead.

=item * C<< $msg->default_max_pods_constraint() >> / C<< $msg->default_max_pods_constraint($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::MaxPodsConstraint>)

The default constraint on the maximum number of pods that can be run
simultaneously on a node in the node pool of this cluster. Only honored
if cluster created with IP Alias support.

=item * C<< $msg->resource_usage_export_config() >> / C<< $msg->resource_usage_export_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::ResourceUsageExportConfig>)

Configuration for exporting resource usages. Resource usage export is
disabled when this config unspecified.

=item * C<< $msg->authenticator_groups_config() >> / C<< $msg->authenticator_groups_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::AuthenticatorGroupsConfig>)

Configuration controlling RBAC group membership information.

=item * C<< $msg->private_cluster_config() >> / C<< $msg->private_cluster_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::PrivateClusterConfig>)

Configuration for private cluster.

=item * C<< $msg->vertical_pod_autoscaling() >> / C<< $msg->vertical_pod_autoscaling($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::VerticalPodAutoscaling>)

Cluster-level Vertical Pod Autoscaling configuration.

=item * C<< $msg->shielded_nodes() >> / C<< $msg->shielded_nodes($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::ShieldedNodes>)

Shielded Nodes configuration.

=item * C<< $msg->release_channel() >> / C<< $msg->release_channel($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::ReleaseChannel>)

Release channel configuration. If left unspecified on cluster creation and
a version is specified, the cluster is enrolled in the most mature release
channel where the version is available (first checking STABLE, then
REGULAR, and finally RAPID). Otherwise, if no release channel
configuration and no version is specified, the cluster is enrolled in the
REGULAR channel with its default version.

=item * C<< $msg->workload_identity_config() >> / C<< $msg->workload_identity_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::WorkloadIdentityConfig>)

Configuration for the use of Kubernetes Service Accounts in IAM policies.

=item * C<< $msg->workload_certificates() >> / C<< $msg->workload_certificates($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::WorkloadCertificates>)

Configuration for issuance of mTLS keys and certificates to Kubernetes
pods.

=item * C<< $msg->mesh_certificates() >> / C<< $msg->mesh_certificates($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::MeshCertificates>)

Configuration for issuance of mTLS keys and certificates to Kubernetes
pods.

=item * C<< $msg->workload_alts_config() >> / C<< $msg->workload_alts_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::WorkloadALTSConfig>)

Configuration for direct-path (via ALTS) with workload identity. This
feature is not officially supported for external customers in Kubernetes
Engine when using Workload Identity.

=item * C<< $msg->cost_management_config() >> / C<< $msg->cost_management_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::CostManagementConfig>)

Configuration for the fine-grained cost management feature.

=item * C<< $msg->cluster_telemetry() >> / C<< $msg->cluster_telemetry($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::ClusterTelemetry>)

Telemetry integration for the cluster.

=item * C<< $msg->tpu_config() >> / C<< $msg->tpu_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::TpuConfig>)

Configuration for Cloud TPU support;
This field is deprecated due to the deprecation of 2VM TPU. The end of life
date for 2VM TPU is 2025-04-25.

