NodeKubeletConfig controls the defaults for new node-pools.

Currently only `insecure_kubelet_readonly_port_enabled` can be set here.

=back

=head2 Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::NodePoolAutoConfig

node pool configs that apply to all auto-provisioned node pools
in autopilot clusters and node auto-provisioning enabled clusters

Inherits from L<Protobuf::Message>.

=head3 Accessors

=over 4

=item * C<< $msg->network_tags() >> / C<< $msg->network_tags($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::NetworkTags>)

The list of instance tags applied to all nodes. Tags are used to identify
valid sources or targets for network firewalls and are specified by
the client during cluster creation. Each tag within the list
must comply with RFC1035.

=item * C<< $msg->resource_manager_tags() >> / C<< $msg->resource_manager_tags($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::ResourceManagerTags>)

Resource manager tag keys and values to be attached to the nodes
for managing Compute Engine firewalls using Network Firewall Policies.

=item * C<< $msg->node_kubelet_config() >> / C<< $msg->node_kubelet_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::NodeKubeletConfig>)

NodeKubeletConfig controls the defaults for autoprovisioned node-pools.

Currently only `insecure_kubelet_readonly_port_enabled` can be set here.

=item * C<< $msg->linux_node_config() >> / C<< $msg->linux_node_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::LinuxNodeConfig>)

Output only. Configuration options for Linux nodes.

=back

=head2 Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::ClusterUpdate

ClusterUpdate describes an update to the cluster. Exactly one update can
be applied to a cluster with each request, so at most one field can be
provided.

Inherits from L<Protobuf::Message>.

=head3 Accessors

=over 4

=item * C<< $msg->desired_node_version() >> / C<< $msg->desired_node_version($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The Kubernetes version to change the nodes to (typically an
upgrade).

Users may specify either explicit versions offered by
Kubernetes Engine or version aliases, which have the following behavior:

- "latest": picks the highest valid Kubernetes version
- "1.X": picks the highest valid patch+gke.N patch in the 1.X version
- "1.X.Y": picks the highest valid gke.N patch in the 1.X.Y version
- "1.X.Y-gke.N": picks an explicit Kubernetes version
- "-": picks the Kubernetes master version

=item * C<< $msg->desired_monitoring_service() >> / C<< $msg->desired_monitoring_service($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The monitoring service the cluster should use to write metrics.
Currently available options:

* `monitoring.googleapis.com/kubernetes` - The Cloud Monitoring
service with a Kubernetes-native resource model
* `monitoring.googleapis.com` - The legacy Cloud Monitoring service (no
  longer available as of GKE 1.15).
* `none` - No metrics will be exported from the cluster.

If left as an empty string,`monitoring.googleapis.com/kubernetes` will be
used for GKE 1.14+ or `monitoring.googleapis.com` for earlier versions.

=item * C<< $msg->desired_addons_config() >> / C<< $msg->desired_addons_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::AddonsConfig>)

Configurations for the various addons available to run in the cluster.

=item * C<< $msg->desired_node_pool_id() >> / C<< $msg->desired_node_pool_id($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The node pool to be upgraded. This field is mandatory if
"desired_node_version", "desired_image_family",
"desired_node_pool_autoscaling", or "desired_workload_metadata_config"
is specified and there is more than one node pool on the cluster.

=item * C<< $msg->desired_image_type() >> / C<< $msg->desired_image_type($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The desired image type for the node pool.
NOTE: Set the "desired_node_pool" field as well.

=item * C<< $msg->desired_node_pool_autoscaling() >> / C<< $msg->desired_node_pool_autoscaling($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::NodePoolAutoscaling>)

Autoscaler configuration for the node pool specified in
desired_node_pool_id. If there is only one pool in the
cluster and desired_node_pool_id is not provided then
the change applies to that single node pool.

=item * C<< $msg->desired_locations() >> / C<< $msg->desired_locations($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The desired list of Google Compute Engine
[zones](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/zones#available)
in which the cluster's nodes should be located.

This list must always include the cluster's primary zone.

Warning: changing cluster locations will update the locations of all node
pools and will result in nodes being added and/or removed.

=item * C<< $msg->desired_master_authorized_networks_config() >> / C<< $msg->desired_master_authorized_networks_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::MasterAuthorizedNetworksConfig>)

The desired configuration options for master authorized networks feature.

Deprecated: Use
desired_control_plane_endpoints_config.ip_endpoints_config.authorized_networks_config
instead.

=item * C<< $msg->desired_pod_security_policy_config() >> / C<< $msg->desired_pod_security_policy_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::PodSecurityPolicyConfig>)

The desired configuration options for the PodSecurityPolicy feature.

=item * C<< $msg->desired_cluster_autoscaling() >> / C<< $msg->desired_cluster_autoscaling($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::ClusterAutoscaling>)

Cluster-level autoscaling configuration.

=item * C<< $msg->desired_binary_authorization() >> / C<< $msg->desired_binary_authorization($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::BinaryAuthorization>)

The desired configuration options for the Binary Authorization feature.

=item * C<< $msg->desired_logging_service() >> / C<< $msg->desired_logging_service($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The logging service the cluster should use to write logs.
Currently available options:

* `logging.googleapis.com/kubernetes` - The Cloud Logging
service with a Kubernetes-native resource model
* `logging.googleapis.com` - The legacy Cloud Logging service (no longer
  available as of GKE 1.15).
* `none` - no logs will be exported from the cluster.

If left as an empty string,`logging.googleapis.com/kubernetes` will be
used for GKE 1.14+ or `logging.googleapis.com` for earlier versions.

=item * C<< $msg->desired_resource_usage_export_config() >> / C<< $msg->desired_resource_usage_export_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::ResourceUsageExportConfig>)

The desired configuration for exporting resource usage.

=item * C<< $msg->desired_vertical_pod_autoscaling() >> / C<< $msg->desired_vertical_pod_autoscaling($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::VerticalPodAutoscaling>)

Cluster-level Vertical Pod Autoscaling configuration.

=item * C<< $msg->desired_private_cluster_config() >> / C<< $msg->desired_private_cluster_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::PrivateClusterConfig>)

The desired private cluster configuration. master_global_access_config is
the only field that can be changed via this field.
See also
[ClusterUpdate.desired_enable_private_endpoint][google.container.v1beta1.ClusterUpdate.desired_enable_private_endpoint]
for modifying other fields within
[PrivateClusterConfig][google.container.v1beta1.PrivateClusterConfig].

Deprecated: Use
desired_control_plane_endpoints_config.ip_endpoints_config.global_access
instead.

=item * C<< $msg->desired_intra_node_visibility_config() >> / C<< $msg->desired_intra_node_visibility_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::IntraNodeVisibilityConfig>)

The desired config of Intra-node visibility.

=item * C<< $msg->desired_default_snat_status() >> / C<< $msg->desired_default_snat_status($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::DefaultSnatStatus>)

The desired status of whether to disable default sNAT for this cluster.

=item * C<< $msg->desired_cluster_telemetry() >> / C<< $msg->desired_cluster_telemetry($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::ClusterTelemetry>)

The desired telemetry integration for the cluster.

=item * C<< $msg->desired_release_channel() >> / C<< $msg->desired_release_channel($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::ReleaseChannel>)

The desired release channel configuration.

=item * C<< $msg->private_cluster_config() >> / C<< $msg->private_cluster_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::PrivateClusterConfig>)

The desired private cluster configuration. Has no effect. Use
[desired_private_cluster_config][google.container.v1beta1.ClusterUpdate.desired_private_cluster_config]
instead.

=item * C<< $msg->desired_tpu_config() >> / C<< $msg->desired_tpu_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::TpuConfig>)

The desired Cloud TPU configuration.
This field is deprecated due to the deprecation of 2VM TPU. The end of life
date for 2VM TPU is 2025-04-25.

=item * C<< $msg->desired_l4ilb_subsetting_config() >> / C<< $msg->desired_l4ilb_subsetting_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::ILBSubsettingConfig>)

The desired L4 Internal Load Balancer Subsetting configuration.

=item * C<< $msg->desired_datapath_provider() >> / C<< $msg->desired_datapath_provider($value) >>

Type: C<Enum> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::DatapathProvider>)

The desired datapath provider for the cluster.

=item * C<< $msg->desired_private_ipv6_google_access() >> / C<< $msg->desired_private_ipv6_google_access($value) >>

Type: C<Enum> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::PrivateIPv6GoogleAccess>)

The desired state of IPv6 connectivity to Google Services.

=item * C<< $msg->desired_notification_config() >> / C<< $msg->desired_notification_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::NotificationConfig>)

The desired notification configuration.

=item * C<< $msg->desired_master_version() >> / C<< $msg->desired_master_version($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The Kubernetes version to change the master to. The only valid value is the
latest supported version.

Users may specify either explicit versions offered by
Kubernetes Engine or version aliases, which have the following behavior:

- "latest": picks the highest valid Kubernetes version
- "1.X": picks the highest valid patch+gke.N patch in the 1.X version
- "1.X.Y": picks the highest valid gke.N patch in the 1.X.Y version
- "1.X.Y-gke.N": picks an explicit Kubernetes version
- "-": picks the default Kubernetes version

=item * C<< $msg->desired_gcfs_config() >> / C<< $msg->desired_gcfs_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::GcfsConfig>)

The desired GCFS config for the cluster.

=item * C<< $msg->desired_image() >> / C<< $msg->desired_image($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The desired name of the image to use for this node.
This is used to create clusters using a custom image.

=item * C<< $msg->desired_image_project() >> / C<< $msg->desired_image_project($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The project containing the desired image to use for this node.
This is used to create clusters using a custom image.

=item * C<< $msg->desired_database_encryption() >> / C<< $msg->desired_database_encryption($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::DatabaseEncryption>)

Configuration of etcd encryption.

=item * C<< $msg->desired_workload_identity_config() >> / C<< $msg->desired_workload_identity_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::WorkloadIdentityConfig>)

Configuration for Workload Identity.

=item * C<< $msg->desired_workload_certificates() >> / C<< $msg->desired_workload_certificates($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::WorkloadCertificates>)

Configuration for issuance of mTLS keys and certificates to Kubernetes
pods.

=item * C<< $msg->desired_mesh_certificates() >> / C<< $msg->desired_mesh_certificates($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::MeshCertificates>)

Configuration for issuance of mTLS keys and certificates to Kubernetes
pods.

=item * C<< $msg->desired_workload_alts_config() >> / C<< $msg->desired_workload_alts_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::WorkloadALTSConfig>)

Configuration for direct-path (via ALTS) with workload identity. This
