=head2 Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::UpdateNodePoolRequest

SetNodePoolVersionRequest updates the version of a node pool.

Inherits from L<Protobuf::Message>.

=head3 Accessors

=over 4

=item * C<< $msg->project_id() >> / C<< $msg->project_id($value) >>

Type: C<String>

Deprecated. The Google Developers Console [project ID or project
number](https://cloud.google.com/resource-manager/docs/creating-managing-projects).
This field has been deprecated and replaced by the name field.

=item * C<< $msg->zone() >> / C<< $msg->zone($value) >>

Type: C<String>

Deprecated. The name of the Google Compute Engine
[zone](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/zones#available)
in which the cluster resides. This field has been deprecated and replaced
by the name field.

=item * C<< $msg->cluster_id() >> / C<< $msg->cluster_id($value) >>

Type: C<String>

Deprecated. The name of the cluster to upgrade.
This field has been deprecated and replaced by the name field.

=item * C<< $msg->node_pool_id() >> / C<< $msg->node_pool_id($value) >>

Type: C<String>

Deprecated. The name of the node pool to upgrade.
This field has been deprecated and replaced by the name field.

=item * C<< $msg->node_version() >> / C<< $msg->node_version($value) >>

Type: C<String>

Required. The Kubernetes version to change the nodes to (typically an
upgrade).

Users may specify either explicit versions offered by Kubernetes Engine or
version aliases, which have the following behavior:

- "latest": picks the highest valid Kubernetes version
- "1.X": picks the highest valid patch+gke.N patch in the 1.X version
- "1.X.Y": picks the highest valid gke.N patch in the 1.X.Y version
- "1.X.Y-gke.N": picks an explicit Kubernetes version
- "-": picks the Kubernetes master version

=item * C<< $msg->image_type() >> / C<< $msg->image_type($value) >>

Type: C<String>

Required. The desired image type for the node pool. Please see
https://cloud.google.com/kubernetes-engine/docs/concepts/node-images
for available image types.

=item * C<< $msg->image() >> / C<< $msg->image($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The desired name of the image name to use for this node.
This is used to create clusters using a custom image.

=item * C<< $msg->image_project() >> / C<< $msg->image_project($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The project containing the desired image to use for this node pool.
This is used to create clusters using a custom image.

=item * C<< $msg->locations() >> / C<< $msg->locations($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The desired list of Google Compute Engine
[zones](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/zones#available)
in which the node pool's nodes should be located. Changing the locations
for a node pool will result in nodes being either created or removed from
the node pool, depending on whether locations are being added or removed.

Warning: It is recommended to update node pool locations in a standalone
API call. Do not combine a location update with changes to other fields
(such as `tags`, `labels`, `taints`, etc.) in the same request.
Otherwise, the API performs a structural modification where changes to
other fields will only apply to newly created nodes and will not be
applied to existing nodes in the node pool. To ensure all nodes are updated
consistently, use a separate API call for location changes.

=item * C<< $msg->workload_metadata_config() >> / C<< $msg->workload_metadata_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::WorkloadMetadataConfig>)

The desired workload metadata config for the node pool.

=item * C<< $msg->name() >> / C<< $msg->name($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The name (project, location, cluster, node pool) of the node pool to
update. Specified in the format
`projects/*/locations/*/clusters/*/nodePools/*`.

=item * C<< $msg->upgrade_settings() >> / C<< $msg->upgrade_settings($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::NodePool::UpgradeSettings>)

Upgrade settings control disruption and speed of the upgrade.

=item * C<< $msg->tags() >> / C<< $msg->tags($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::NetworkTags>)

The desired network tags to be applied to all nodes in the node pool.
If this field is not present, the tags will not be changed. Otherwise,
the existing network tags will be *replaced* with the provided tags.

=item * C<< $msg->taints() >> / C<< $msg->taints($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::NodeTaints>)

The desired node taints to be applied to all nodes in the node pool.
If this field is not present, the taints will not be changed. Otherwise,
the existing node taints will be *replaced* with the provided taints.

=item * C<< $msg->labels() >> / C<< $msg->labels($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::NodeLabels>)

The desired node labels to be applied to all nodes in the node pool.
If this field is not present, the labels will not be changed. Otherwise,
the existing node labels will be *replaced* with the provided labels.

=item * C<< $msg->linux_node_config() >> / C<< $msg->linux_node_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::LinuxNodeConfig>)

Parameters that can be configured on Linux nodes.

=item * C<< $msg->kubelet_config() >> / C<< $msg->kubelet_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::NodeKubeletConfig>)

Node kubelet configs.

=item * C<< $msg->node_network_config() >> / C<< $msg->node_network_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::NodeNetworkConfig>)

Node network config.

=item * C<< $msg->gcfs_config() >> / C<< $msg->gcfs_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::GcfsConfig>)

GCFS config.

=item * C<< $msg->confidential_nodes() >> / C<< $msg->confidential_nodes($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::ConfidentialNodes>)

Confidential nodes config.
All the nodes in the node pool will be Confidential VM once enabled.

=item * C<< $msg->gvnic() >> / C<< $msg->gvnic($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::VirtualNIC>)

Enable or disable gvnic on the node pool.

=item * C<< $msg->etag() >> / C<< $msg->etag($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The current etag of the node pool.
If an etag is provided and does not match the current etag of the node
pool, update will be blocked and an ABORTED error will be returned.

=item * C<< $msg->fast_socket() >> / C<< $msg->fast_socket($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::FastSocket>)

Enable or disable NCCL fast socket for the node pool.

=item * C<< $msg->logging_config() >> / C<< $msg->logging_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::NodePoolLoggingConfig>)

Logging configuration.

=item * C<< $msg->resource_labels() >> / C<< $msg->resource_labels($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::ResourceLabels>)

The resource labels for the node pool to use to annotate any related
Google Compute Engine resources.

=item * C<< $msg->windows_node_config() >> / C<< $msg->windows_node_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::WindowsNodeConfig>)

Parameters that can be configured on Windows nodes.

=item * C<< $msg->accelerators() >> / C<< $msg->accelerators($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::AcceleratorConfig>)

A list of hardware accelerators to be attached to each node.
See
https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/gpus
for more information about support for GPUs.

=item * C<< $msg->machine_type() >> / C<< $msg->machine_type($value) >>

Type: C<String>

