=head3 Accessors

=over 4

=item * C<< $msg->network() >> / C<< $msg->network($value) >>

Type: C<String>

Output only. The relative name of the Google Compute Engine
[network](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/networks-and-firewalls#networks)
to which the cluster is connected. Example:
projects/my-project/global/networks/my-network

=item * C<< $msg->subnetwork() >> / C<< $msg->subnetwork($value) >>

Type: C<String>

Output only. The relative name of the Google Compute Engine
[subnetwork](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/vpc)
to which the cluster is connected. Example:
projects/my-project/regions/us-central1/subnetworks/my-subnet

=item * C<< $msg->enable_intra_node_visibility() >> / C<< $msg->enable_intra_node_visibility($value) >>

Type: C<Bool>

Whether Intra-node visibility is enabled for this cluster.
This makes same node pod to pod traffic visible for VPC network.

=item * C<< $msg->default_snat_status() >> / C<< $msg->default_snat_status($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::DefaultSnatStatus>)

Whether the cluster disables default in-node sNAT rules. In-node sNAT rules
will be disabled when default_snat_status is disabled. When disabled is set
to false, default IP masquerade rules will be applied to the nodes to
prevent sNAT on cluster internal traffic.

=item * C<< $msg->enable_l4ilb_subsetting() >> / C<< $msg->enable_l4ilb_subsetting($value) >>

Type: C<Bool>

Whether L4ILB Subsetting is enabled for this cluster.

=item * C<< $msg->datapath_provider() >> / C<< $msg->datapath_provider($value) >>

Type: C<Enum> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::DatapathProvider>)

The desired datapath provider for this cluster. By default, uses the
IPTables-based kube-proxy implementation.

=item * C<< $msg->private_ipv6_google_access() >> / C<< $msg->private_ipv6_google_access($value) >>

Type: C<Enum> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::PrivateIPv6GoogleAccess>)

The desired state of IPv6 connectivity to Google Services.
By default, no private IPv6 access to or from Google Services (all access
will be via IPv4)

=item * C<< $msg->dns_config() >> / C<< $msg->dns_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::DNSConfig>)

DNSConfig contains clusterDNS config for this cluster.

=item * C<< $msg->service_external_ips_config() >> / C<< $msg->service_external_ips_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::ServiceExternalIPsConfig>)

ServiceExternalIPsConfig specifies if services with externalIPs field are
blocked or not.

=item * C<< $msg->gateway_api_config() >> / C<< $msg->gateway_api_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::GatewayAPIConfig>)

GatewayAPIConfig contains the desired config of Gateway API on this
cluster.

=item * C<< $msg->enable_multi_networking() >> / C<< $msg->enable_multi_networking($value) >>

Type: C<Bool>

Whether multi-networking is enabled for this cluster.

=item * C<< $msg->network_performance_config() >> / C<< $msg->network_performance_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::NetworkConfig::ClusterNetworkPerformanceConfig>)

Network bandwidth tier configuration.

=item * C<< $msg->enable_fqdn_network_policy() >> / C<< $msg->enable_fqdn_network_policy($value) >>

Type: C<Bool>

Whether FQDN Network Policy is enabled on this cluster.

=item * C<< $msg->in_transit_encryption_config() >> / C<< $msg->in_transit_encryption_config($value) >>

Type: C<Enum> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::InTransitEncryptionConfig>)

Specify the details of in-transit encryption.

=item * C<< $msg->enable_cilium_clusterwide_network_policy() >> / C<< $msg->enable_cilium_clusterwide_network_policy($value) >>

Type: C<Bool>

Whether CiliumClusterWideNetworkPolicy is enabled on this cluster.

=item * C<< $msg->default_enable_private_nodes() >> / C<< $msg->default_enable_private_nodes($value) >>

Type: C<Bool>

Controls whether by default nodes have private IP addresses only.
It is invalid to specify both [PrivateClusterConfig.enablePrivateNodes][]
and this field at the same time.
To update the default setting, use
[ClusterUpdate.desired_default_enable_private_nodes][google.container.v1beta1.ClusterUpdate.desired_default_enable_private_nodes]

=item * C<< $msg->dataplane_v2_config() >> / C<< $msg->dataplane_v2_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Container::V1beta1::ClusterService::DataplaneV2Config>)

Optional. DataplaneV2Config specifies the DPv2 configuration.

=item * C<< $msg->disable_l4_lb_firewall_reconciliation() >> / C<< $msg->disable_l4_lb_firewall_reconciliation($value) >>

Type: C<Bool>

Disable L4 load balancer VPC firewalls to enable firewall policies.

=back

